In Montague's program, an intension is just the function that maps
world-time indexes to extensions.  So for a one-place predicate like
{nanmu}, the intension expressed by {lo nanmu} gives you a set of
mundane {nanmu}s at each word-time index.  You get the extension that
you want by specifying or glorking the world and time.  Is this
something like what you have in mind when you say "maximal bunches"?

